      "rationale": "The direct oracle corresponds to the scoped caller responsibility. AppendFuture.Response explicitly requires Error to have returned and restricts response validity to success; Future.Error supplies the completion status. These interface statements apply because pipelineDecode consumes AppendFuture directly. The wording distinguishes access ordering from successful-result validity, but the checked decoder immediately interprets the returned response, so requiring prior nil status is appropriate here. Both observed witnesses also violate the unambiguous ordering requirement independently: neither future received any Error call. The attached implementation calls Request and Response before inspecting Term and Success. In actual check 74f4f14b61644bce8ce450d9be521137, response_access events 2 and 7 report zero Error calls and false validation, each correlated by operation_id with its own completed input. Both decoder_completed events independently retain zero Error calls and one Response call. Thus the trigger was actually reached; the discrepancy is not inferred from a checker identifier or test exit status. The instrumented methods measure actual consumer calls without replacing the consumer or deriving validation from response fields. The unbuffered handoff selects the future before shutdown is requested, and finishCh synchronizes final field reads. A future_delivered log appearing after response_access is consistent with sender scheduling after handoff and does not invalidate delivery. Equal terms, empty entries, and an empty notification map avoid unsupported helper dependencies on these paths. Consumer delivery can provide completion and visibility, but the network producer calls respond(err) and can deliver the future without filtering errors; delivery therefore does not replace status validation. Fresh response allocation and the Success guard can prevent endpoint updates for failed responses, but cannot satisfy the prior-access requirement. The Go test's PASS records successful observation collection, while the supplied event assertion detects the local contract mismatch. Conversely, satisfying this access obligation would still leave peer attribution, response semantics, and replication-context ownership unresolved, so it is insufficient to establish the broader voter-progress guarantee. No correspondence issue was found within this bounded direct check.",
